Expand each shared node once in R_cycle_detected(), so the eval target
stops timing out on assignments of values with shared subexpressions.

R_FixupRHS() calls R_cycle_detected() (src/main/duplicate.c) before
`$<-`, `[[<-`, the byte-code setter and `attr<-` replace an existing
element.  It walked every path through the value instead of every node,
so its time doubled with each level of sharing, and a value reaching
itself through an environment's attributes overflowed the C stack.
Remember the nodes with REFCNT > 1, and the root, in a pointer set and
expand each once (oss-fuzz testcase 5562094521745408: a 112-byte input
that keeps storing x in its own elements; a 60 s timeout before, 3.4 s
under ASan with this patch).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #483 (no Bugzilla report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

